      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is no light at the end of the shift, but there is also no point in stopping the very thing that keeps you alive. The exhaustion you feel is not a sign to quit, but a signal that you are carrying a burden so heavy it requires a different kind of strength than running. You do not have to keep moving forward to find peace; sometimes, the only way to stop the pain is to let the weight rest on the floor and breathe.",
      "source": "target",
